    "body": "With more than one param group, ZeRO-1/2 can't read or write the optimizer state of any group after the first:\n\n```python\n# two groups, e.g. weight decay on/off\nsafe_get_full_optimizer_state(bias, \"exp_avg\")\n# ValueError: exp_avg not found in optimizer state fragment\n```\n\nWith two ranks only the rank holding the param raises, and the other one hangs when it reads the result.\n\nThe cause is the lazy linking from #5104. `_optimizer_step` steps the groups one at a time, but all of them get linked right after the first group's step, when the rest have no state yet, and it never runs again. It worked before #5104, and ZeRO-3 is fine.\n\nThis links each group after its own step instead.\n\nThe fragment tests only ever used one group, so I added `TestTensorFragmentOptimizerStatePerGroup` with two groups, which compares `exp_avg` and `exp_avg_sq` against plain PyTorch AdamW. It fails on master and passes here. Fragment and checkpoint tests pass on 2×H20 (174 passed).\n\n\n## Environment\n\nNVIDIA H20-3e, driver 580.105.08, Python 3.11.15, torch 2.9.1+cu128; the runs above used 2 GPUs.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
