      "body": "<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n## Copilot review overview\n\n### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe focused fix matches ZeRO-1/2’s sequential group stepping and includes appropriate regression coverage.\n\n**Review effort:** Balanced  \n**Findings:** None\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nFixes ZeRO-1/2 optimizer-state access for models with multiple parameter groups.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Tracks optimizer-state linkage per parameter group.\n- Links each group immediately after its first optimizer step.\n- Adds multi-group regression coverage across ZeRO stages and CPU offload.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `deepspeed/​runtime/​zero/​stage_1_and_2.py` | Implements per-group lazy optimizer-state linking. |\r\n| `tests/​unit/​runtime/​zero/​test_zero_tensor_fragment.py` | Verifies AdamW state access for two parameter groups. |\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/new/master?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>",
